<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Barlow Ridge</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:180-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.282436" lon="-121.685554"><ele>1267.4</ele><name>Barlow Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:barlow-pass-sno-park (OSM way 129814976); confidence: high; pdf_page: 180; book_elev_ft: 4157; quote: map 39: BARLOW PASS 4157'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.281850" lon="-121.680830"><ele>1205.3</ele><name>Devils Half Acre / Barlow Butte trails junction</name><desc>source: OSM: west end of Barlow Butte Trail #670 way 523155350, north end of Devil's Half Acre Trail #482A way 129815181, by the sno-park; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 179; quote: From Barlow Pass Sno-Park descend the Devils Half Acre Trail 250 yards</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.281780" lon="-121.677020"><ele>1251.5</ele><name>Mineral Jane Ski Trail, west end</name><desc>source: OSM: east end of Barlow Butte Trail #670 way 523155350 = west end of Mineral Jane Ski Trail way 548899767; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 179; quote: From Barlow Pass Sno-Park descend the Devils Half Acre Trail 250 yards, then turn left onto the Mineral Jane Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.281800" lon="-121.675260"><ele>1256.5</ele><name>Mineral Jane Ski Trail, east end</name><desc>source: OSM way 548899767 east end (the mapped 0.1 mi of the trail); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 180; quote: down a difficult, often nasty, and steep section of the old Barlow Road to a small meadow. Go left and climb a forested hillside ... to a series of clearcuts and road that leads to Barlow Saddle</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.282810" lon="-121.669570"><ele>1233.8</ele><name>Barlow Saddle (Road 3560 where the Mineral Jane track joins)</name><desc>source: OSM: east end of unnamed track 40771991 on Forest Road 3560 way 5039387, in the saddle; DEM 4,047 ft (the road's low point, 4,027 ft, is 130 m north at the 3560-220/221 forks); confidence: high; pdf_page: 179; book_elev_ft: 4000; quote: Barlow Saddle (4,000 feet) is a wide, clearcut saddle at the west base of Barlow Ridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.273920" lon="-121.648000"><ele>1432.3</ele><name>High point curve (4,730 ft viewpoint)</name><desc>source: OSM Forest Road 3560 hairpin, DEM 4,699 ft, 1.54 mi by road from the saddle; confidence: high; pdf_page: 182; book_elev_ft: 4730; quote: climbing steadily and gently ... for 1.6 miles to the high point (4,730 feet), where the road makes a sharp turn, levels out, and passes the first clearcut</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.262090" lon="-121.640020"><ele>1378.5</ele><name>Turnaround, 2.8 mi from the saddle</name><desc>source: OSM Forest Road 3560, about 2.8 mi by road from the saddle; the OSM road goes on 0.3 mi more, descending to 4,478 ft; confidence: low; pdf_page: 182; quote: This Intermediate tour can extend up to 2.8 miles one way ... then continues on the level through several clearcuts to a dead end</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Barlow Ridge</name><desc>1. Barlow Pass Sno-Park -&gt; Devils Half Acre / Barlow Butte trails junction: straight (medium), 0.23 mi | 2. Devils Half Acre / Barlow Butte trails junction -&gt; Mineral Jane Ski Trail, west end: osm (medium), 0.23 mi | 3. Mineral Jane Ski Trail, west end -&gt; Mineral Jane Ski Trail, east end: osm (medium), 0.10 mi | 4. Mineral Jane Ski Trail, east end -&gt; Barlow Saddle (Road 3560 where the Mineral Jane track joins): osm (low), 0.31 mi | 5. Barlow Saddle (Road 3560 where the Mineral Jane track joins) -&gt; High point curve (4,730 ft viewpoint): osm (high), 1.51 mi | 6. High point curve (4,730 ft viewpoint) -&gt; Turnaround, 2.8 mi from the saddle: osm (medium), 1.41 mi</desc>
